# Project conventions

## Stack and deployment

- Vite + vanilla strict TypeScript. No UI framework or heavy component library.
- Static installable PWA deployed to `xgrybvo6508-dot/social-agents` on GitHub Pages.
- Vite `base` is `/social-agents/`. Use `import.meta.env.BASE_URL` for asset and navigation paths.
- Bundle everything locally. No third-party fonts, CDNs, trackers, analytics, or runtime dependencies on a server.
- Tooling: Vitest, ESLint with typescript-eslint, and Prettier.

## Layout

```text
src/
  main.ts     # bootstrap only
  agent/      # provider settings, API client, prompts, schemas, validation
  memory/     # IndexedDB, migrations, import/export, phrase SRS
  modes/      # phrase prep/training, helper, task extraction, TA workflows
  content/    # starter phrases, TA cards, manual worksheets
  ui/         # semantic views, components, CSS, accessibility
  lib/        # small pure helpers, Result/types/guards
```

Tests are colocated as `*.test.ts`.

## Engineering rules

- Enable `strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`, and `noImplicitOverride`. Never use `any`; validate `unknown` at boundaries.
- Prefer named exports, small pure modules, dependency injection for fetch/storage/time, and one responsibility per file (roughly under 200 lines).
- Keep DOM and persistence out of core logic. Use typed errors and calm, actionable UI messages.
- Memory lives in versioned IndexedDB stores for people, groups, roles, phrases, sessions, and saved tasks/fixations. Migrate without silently losing data.
- Settings alone use localStorage key `sa:settings`. JSON export/import includes memory, never settings or keys.
- Without an API key, every mode still has a guided manual worksheet; starter phrases, TA cards, and phrase training work offline.

## Required scripts and checks

Keep `dev`, `build`, `preview`, `test`, `lint`, `typecheck`, and `format`. `build` must typecheck before Vite builds.

Before completion run: `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test && npm run build`.
